Specular patch to resvg 0.48.1 (src/filter/morphology.rs): feMorphology in linear time.

What it changes
  Upstream visits every cell of the (2rx x 2ry) kernel for every pixel. The rectangular
  minimum/maximum is separable, so the filter now runs as a row pass and a column pass, each
  with the van Herk/Gil-Werman running block minimum/maximum: three comparisons per pixel and
  channel whatever the radius. Pixels outside the image are the operator's identity, which is
  what upstream's skipping amounts to; the result is identical (unit test against the direct
  form over random images, radii and both operators).

Why
  Found by the real-world shakedown: resvg's own feMorphology tests (radius 10 in a 200-unit
  viewBox) rendered at the viewer's 2048-pixel size took longer than the 60 s budget, one
  render thread busy the whole time.

